# Epoch sessions

Read `PRODUCT.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/EXECUTION.md`. If this chat names a brief, read that file next and stop. Do not re-explore the repo. `docs/polish/`, `THESIS.md`, roadmaps, and `tasks/` are archive unless a contract or brief cites a specific passage.

One Work Unit per chat. Finish it. Do not start the next unit in the same session.

Priority is only `docs/EXECUTION.md`. Do not resume isolated renderer polish (lighting, sea state, extra fauna, atmosphere identity) unless the integrated proof sequence demonstrates a failure that needs it.

Say "ready for owner verdict," never "accepted," for pixels, motion, or assets. Automated tests do not pass visual or causal gates.

WebGPU works on the owner's machine. Never conclude the renderer is broken from headless capture, a throttled browser pane, or `--enable-unsafe-webgpu`. Do not report fps from those environments.

Install workaround until the lockfile unit lands: `npm install --no-package-lock --no-save`.
